
# Phoneme chart — the sound inventory of a constructed language as a grid of phoneme cells. A reusable widget a
# package document embeds. Headless (data-slot hooks, style via CSS). Props:
#   sounds -> list of { symbol, label }; `symbol` is the IPA / script glyph, `label` the description (e.g. "voiced
#             bilabial nasal"). Group and lay out via CSS on [data-slot=phoneme-chart].

load @term/site/code/zone/render
  find element
  find text
load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append

zone phoneme-chart
  take host, like view
  take sounds
  zone div
    bind data-slot, text <phoneme-chart>
    walk list, read sounds
      hook next
        take site, name sound
        zone div
          bind data-slot, text <phoneme>
          zone span
            bind data-slot, text <phoneme-symbol>
            read
              read sound/symbol
          zone span
            bind data-slot, text <phoneme-label>
            read
              read sound/label
